"""PROPOSAL ONLY -- not committed as an active migration, not applied anywhere.
Kept as .draft so Alembic never auto-loads it; rename to .py and get sign-off,
then re-verify in an isolated database, before activation.

Chain position changed again this round: now rebases onto 0009 (field-test
participants draft) instead of 0007 directly, so that field-test can be
activated and applied on its own without requiring Web Push -- the two
drafts have no DB-content dependency on each other; this was purely a
chain-ordering coupling from an earlier round. The three proposals still
form a single linear chain, just reordered: 0006 -> 0007 -> 0009 -> 0008,
with no new Alembic heads. If/when Web Push is activated it will still
require 0009 to be applied first (chain-wise), independent of the
credential-rotation question below.

Schema fixed this round: the already-committed app/api/jiaan_webpush_routes.py
and app/services/jiaan_webpush.py (commit 0a3d16a) insert/lookup/ON CONFLICT
against an `endpoint_hash` column on jiaan_webpush_subscriptions that this
draft's CREATE TABLE never declared, and ON CONFLICT (endpoint_hash) has no
matching UNIQUE constraint to target -- applying the old draft as-is would
make `subscribe()` fail at runtime with "no unique or exclusion constraint
matching the ON CONFLICT specification" (or "column endpoint_hash does not
exist"). Also, `endpoint` is stored encrypted (Fernet, non-deterministic per
call) by the committed code, so UNIQUE on the ciphertext column was never
meaningful; uniqueness must live on the deterministic HMAC `endpoint_hash`
instead. Both are fixed in the DDL below. See
tests/test_jiaan_webpush_migration_consistency_unit.py for the static check
that keeps this draft in sync with the committed call sites going forward.

Fully additive (CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS / CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS), no
ALTER of any existing table, no data deletion. NOT re-verified in a database
this round (no new DB connections made while the credential-rotation status
is unconfirmed); an earlier round reported verifying an isolated-DB draft,
but that was before this schema fix, so the earlier verification no longer
applies to the current DDL and must be redone once activated.

CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS safety gap fixed this round: if a table with
either name already exists -- most plausibly from someone having manually
run the older, buggy deploy/fieldtest/jiaan_webpush_schema.sql (the
"successful one-device test" referenced in app/services/jiaan_webpush.py,
which this session could not confirm or rule out without a database
connection) -- IF NOT EXISTS silently does nothing, leaving that old,
incomplete structure in place while Alembic still records this revision as
applied. upgrade() now re-reads each table's actual columns and unique
constraints after the CREATE statements and raises immediately if they
don't match what the committed application code requires. It never DROPs,
ALTERs, or overwrites anything by itself -- a mismatch stops the migration
with a message telling a human what to check.
"""
from alembic import op
import sqlalchemy as sa


def _columns(conn, table: str) -> set[str]:
    return {row[0] for row in conn.execute(sa.text(
        "SELECT column_name FROM information_schema.columns WHERE table_name = :t"
    ), {"t": table})}


def _constraint_columns(conn, table: str, constraint_type: str) -> list[set[str]]:
    """每個符合 constraint_type 的限制各自涵蓋哪些欄位（可能有多個同類限制）。"""
    rows = conn.execute(sa.text(
        "SELECT tc.constraint_name, ccu.column_name "
        "FROM information_schema.table_constraints tc "
        "JOIN information_schema.constraint_column_usage ccu "
        "  ON tc.constraint_name = ccu.constraint_name AND tc.table_schema = ccu.table_schema "
        "WHERE tc.table_name = :t AND tc.constraint_type = :ct"
    ), {"t": table, "ct": constraint_type}).all()
    grouped: dict[str, set[str]] = {}
    for name, col in rows:
        grouped.setdefault(name, set()).add(col)
    return list(grouped.values())


def _verify_or_fail(conn, table: str, required_columns: set[str], required_unique: set[str]) -> None:
    existing = _columns(conn, table)
    if not existing:
        raise RuntimeError(f"{table} 建立後仍查無任何欄位，資料庫狀態異常，拒絕繼續，請人工檢查")
    missing = required_columns - existing
    if missing:
        raise RuntimeError(
            f"{table} 已存在但缺少欄位：{sorted(missing)}；"
            "可能是不完整的舊版結構被 CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS 略過建立。"
            "本程式拒絕自動 DROP／ALTER／覆寫既有資料；"
            f"請人工確認 {table} 目前實際結構，視需要備份後手動補齊欄位，"
            "再重新套用此 Migration。"
        )
    if required_unique not in _constraint_columns(conn, table, "UNIQUE"):
        raise RuntimeError(
            f"{table} 缺少涵蓋 {sorted(required_unique)} 的 UNIQUE 限制；"
            "可能是舊版結構遺留。本程式拒絕自動修改限制，請人工確認後處理。"
        )


revision = "0008_jiaan_webpush"
down_revision = "0009_fieldtest_participants"
branch_labels = None
depends_on = None


def upgrade() -> None:
    op.execute("""
        CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS jiaan_webpush_subscriptions (
            id uuid PRIMARY KEY,
            user_id uuid NOT NULL REFERENCES users(id),
            org_id uuid NOT NULL REFERENCES organizations(id),
            endpoint text NOT NULL,
            endpoint_hash text NOT NULL UNIQUE,
            p256dh text NOT NULL,
            auth text NOT NULL,
            is_active boolean NOT NULL DEFAULT true,
            created_at timestamptz NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
            updated_at timestamptz NOT NULL DEFAULT now()
        )
    """)
    op.execute("""
        CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS ix_jiaan_webpush_subs_org
            ON jiaan_webpush_subscriptions(org_id, is_active)
    """)
    op.execute("""
        CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS jiaan_webpush_deliveries (
            id uuid PRIMARY KEY,
            emergency_id uuid NOT NULL REFERENCES jiaan1030_emergencies(id),
            subscription_id uuid NOT NULL REFERENCES jiaan_webpush_subscriptions(id),
            stage text NOT NULL CHECK (stage IN ('new','unacknowledged_60s','unacknowledged_180s')),
            status text NOT NULL DEFAULT 'queued',
            attempts int NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,
            created_at timestamptz NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
            attempted_at timestamptz,
            UNIQUE (emergency_id, subscription_id, stage)
        )
    """)
    op.execute("""
        CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS ix_jiaan_webpush_delivery_q
            ON jiaan_webpush_deliveries(status, created_at)
    """)

    conn = op.get_bind()
    _verify_or_fail(
        conn, "jiaan_webpush_subscriptions",
        {"id", "user_id", "org_id", "endpoint", "endpoint_hash", "p256dh", "auth",
         "is_active", "created_at", "updated_at"},
        {"endpoint_hash"},
    )
    _verify_or_fail(
        conn, "jiaan_webpush_deliveries",
        {"id", "emergency_id", "subscription_id", "stage", "status", "attempts",
         "created_at", "attempted_at"},
        {"emergency_id", "subscription_id", "stage"},
    )


def downgrade() -> None:
    # Intended for genuinely new tables this migration created. If either
    # table turns out to pre-date this migration (see the "one-device test"
    # note above) this would still delete it; a human must confirm that is
    # actually wanted (and that nothing else depends on the existing data)
    # before running this -- never run downgrade() unattended.
    op.drop_table("jiaan_webpush_deliveries")
    op.drop_table("jiaan_webpush_subscriptions")
